## Art Deco vs Edwardian vs Victorian — Era Comparison

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Victorian (1837–1900)</th><th>Edwardian (1901–1915)</th><th>Art Deco (1920–1939)</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Primary metal</strong></td><td>18k yellow gold</td><td>Platinum (new tech)</td><td>Platinum (standard)</td><td>Metal signals era.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Signature detail</strong></td><td>Floral, scrollwork, nature</td><td>Milgrain lace, filigree openwork</td><td>Geometric, hexagonal, baguette</td><td>Visual signature per era.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Side stone shapes</strong></td><td>Pear, oval, cushion</td><td>Round, pear, cushion</td><td>Baguette, trapezoid, half-moon</td><td>Side stones differ clearly.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Shoulder shape</strong></td><td>Curved, floral</td><td>Delicate lace openwork</td><td>Geometric, straight, stepped</td><td>Shoulder shape = era test.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Overall feel</strong></td><td>Romantic, feminine</td><td>Delicate, refined</td><td>Bold, architectural</td><td>Each era has distinct energy.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Example setting</strong></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/romantic-diamond-floral-asymmetrical-twist-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-1-4-ct-tw-item-150352?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">Romantic Floral YG $2,095</a></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/petite-vintage-pave-leaf-diamond-engagement-ring-in-platinum-1-5-ct-tw-item-203308?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">Petite Vintage Leaf Platinum $2,510</a></td><td><a href="https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/vintage-baguette-halo-diamond-engagement-ring-in-platinum-1-2-ct-tw-item-203382?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational">Vintage Baguette Halo Platinum $3,440</a></td><td>Modern reproduction of each era.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** The three vintage eras have clearly different signatures. Victorian = yellow gold + floral curves. Edwardian = platinum + milgrain lace. Art Deco = platinum + geometric baguettes. Mixing elements creates cross-era reproductions — honest designs but not period-authentic.

## Art Deco vs Other Setting Families for Marquise

<table class="dc-custom-table"><thead><tr><th>Setting Family</th><th>Setting Cost</th><th>Aesthetic</th><th>Period Authenticity</th><th>What this means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Art Deco (modern reproduction)</strong></td><td>$1,275–$5,280</td><td>1920s geometric</td><td>Reproduction</td><td>Our pick. Visual period + modern provenance.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Vintage general</strong></td><td>$1,100–$5,495</td><td>Cross-era vintage</td><td>Mixed</td><td>Broader category. See <a href="/vintage-marquise-diamond-ring">vintage guide</a>.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Modern classic solitaire</strong></td><td>$790–$2,850</td><td>Timeless modern</td><td>Not vintage</td><td>Clean modern. See <a href="/marquise-solitaire-engagement-ring">solitaire guide</a>.</td></tr><tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong>Halo (modern)</strong></td><td>$1,255–$5,985</td><td>Contemporary</td><td>Not Art Deco</td><td>Modern halo. See <a href="/marquise-halo-engagement-ring">halo guide</a>.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Pavé (modern)</strong></td><td>$1,190–$4,850</td><td>Fire-focused modern</td><td>Not Art Deco</td><td>See <a href="/marquise-pave-engagement-ring">pavé guide</a>.</td></tr></tbody></table>

**Verdict:** Art Deco is a vintage-era aesthetic. Modern settings (classic solitaire, halo, pavé) read as different design languages. If the Art Deco look is the priority, the modern reproductions in this guide deliver it at honest prices. For broader vintage, see the general vintage marquise guide.

