## How to Verify an Art Deco Marquise Before You Buy

Three checks every ring must pass before you commit.

**Check 1 — Confirm the ring passes 3+ of the 4 Art Deco Signals** (milgrain, geometric side stones, platinum/18k white gold, geometric shoulders). If only 1 or 2 pass, the ring is modern-with-vintage-nods, not Art Deco. Price should reflect that.

**Check 2 — Confirm V-tip centre prongs at order.** Art Deco styling does not reduce tip chip risk. V-tip centre mandatory on marquise. Spec at order — $0 extra on most listings.

**Check 3 — Confirm the centre stone has a current GIA report.** For modern-retail Art Deco settings, this is default. For antique shop Art Deco pieces, demand independent GIA re-certification. [IGI](https://www.igi.org/) and [GIA 4Cs](https://4cs.gia.edu/) verify loose stones.

I run these three checks on any Art Deco marquise purchase. Modern-retail Art Deco settings pass all three easily. Antique shop "Art Deco" pieces often fail Check 1 — buy only from authenticated dealers with provenance.

